{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**Raymond III Count of Tripoli**\n\nRaymond III was Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He succeeded his father Raymond II of Tripoli and his mother Hodierna of Jerusalem ruled as regent during his minority. Raymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Crusader states and the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n**Early life and accession**\n\nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father was assassinated in 1152 when Raymond III was about twelve years old making him Count of Tripoli. Since he was a minor his mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age in 1155. During his early years Tripoli faced threats from Nur ad-Din the Zengid ruler who sought to expand his influence into the County of Tripoli.\n\n**Political career and conflicts**\n\nRaymond III became active in politics and warfare as he matured. He allied with the Byzantine Empire and participated in the campaigns of Manuel I Komnenos against Nur ad-Din. In 1164 Raymond was captured at the Battle of Harim and spent the next ten years imprisoned. During his captivity Tripoli was ruled by his cousin Bertrand who was later succeeded by another cousin Pons. Raymond was released in 1174 after paying a ransom and upon his return he resumed control of Tripoli. He played a key role in the politics of Jerusalem serving as regent for King Baldwin IV from 1174 to 1177. Raymond opposed the influence of Guy of Lusignan who later became king and was involved in the factional struggles within the Crusader states.\n\n**Later years and death**\n\nIn his later years Raymond III continued to be a prominent figure in the Crusader states. He supported the succession of Baldwin V and opposed Guy of Lusignan after Baldwin IVs death. Raymond allied with Raymond of Toulouse and other nobles against Guy. However their rebellion failed and Raymond was forced to submit to Guy. He died in 1187 just before Saladins invasion of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. Raymond III was succeeded by his distant cousin Raymond IV of Tripoli. His death marked the end of an era in the history of the County of Tripoli and the Crusader states.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.22343038022518158}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.31561729311943054}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.00013529339048545808}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0447063110768795}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -7.259582343976945e-05}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -5.364403477869928e-06}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.4187118113040924}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.04629985988140106}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.00027497802511788905}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.271182119846344}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.38389164209365845}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -5.006777428206988e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.0006825978052802384}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0005197366117499769}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -7.867782187531702e-06}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0001652104256208986}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -0.0012153151910752058}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.00014530557382386178}, {"token": " until", "logprob": -0.5231835842132568}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.012605514377355576}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.00010954733443213627}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.003436019876971841}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.00017009719158522785}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.9550132492440753e-05}, {"token": "8", "logprob": -1.4781842764932662e-05}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -0.000161038784426637}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.005333599168807268}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.011208427138626575}, {"toke